1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:55,877
Impel Down, a living hell buried beneath the waves where the world's most notorious prisoners are held.

2
00:02:55,877 --> 00:03:03,877
Yet despite being history's most heavily fortified prison, it has been breached by an upstart pirate named Straw Hat Luffy.

3
00:03:03,877 --> 00:03:09,877
He hopes to free his brother Fire Fist Ace, who is condemned to be executed.

4
00:03:09,877 --> 00:03:14,877
However, he is not the only one to make his way through the prison's iron defenses.

5
00:03:14,877 --> 00:03:17,877
Another breach occurred 20 years before.

6
00:03:17,877 --> 00:03:30,877
The culprit was the first and only man to successfully break out of the legendary prison and see the light of day again.

7
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:35,877
Unbelievable.

8
00:03:35,877 --> 00:03:40,877
That damned lunatic cut off his own legs to escape.

9
00:03:40,877 --> 00:03:53,877
And with this astonishing feat, he wrote his name in the pages of history.

10
00:03:53,877 --> 00:04:00,877
Captain of the dreaded flying pirates, Shiki the Golden Lion.

11
00:04:00,877 --> 00:04:13,877
These events transpired only a matter of days before Luffy and the Straw Hat Pirates faced Shiki himself in battle.

12
00:04:13,877 --> 00:04:20,877
A special presentation related to the movie. A Gold Lion's Ambition on the Move.

13
00:04:20,877 --> 00:04:45,877
Captain, seen your call?

14
00:04:45,877 --> 00:04:47,877
Si, what is it?

15
00:04:47,877 --> 00:04:50,877
There's a call. I think it's from the Big Boss Shiki's people.

16
00:04:58,877 --> 00:05:04,877
About time. Sure kept us waiting. Bring me the transponder snail.

17
00:05:04,877 --> 00:05:06,877
Jaser, right away.

18
00:05:06,877 --> 00:05:10,877
You hear that, Big Bro? We might get to team up with Shiki's crew.

19
00:05:12,877 --> 00:05:15,877
If this pans out, we'll be in the Grande Leagues. Just you wait.

20
00:05:17,877 --> 00:05:18,877
Bye.

21
00:05:18,877 --> 00:05:19,877
Bye.

22
00:05:19,877 --> 00:05:20,877
Bye.

23
00:05:20,877 --> 00:05:21,877
Bye.

24
00:05:21,877 --> 00:05:49,097
Hey, Big Bro, are those happy tears?

25
00:05:49,097 --> 00:05:53,097
Sad tears, the saddest hermano cold.

26
00:05:53,097 --> 00:05:57,097
I'm filled with a beautiful sorrow, and we...

27
00:05:57,097 --> 00:06:02,097
If Senor Siki succeeds in the implementation of his odious machinations,

28
00:06:02,097 --> 00:06:06,097
the world will be drowned in a tidal wave of despair.

29
00:06:06,097 --> 00:06:11,097
Si, when I imagine the thousands of wailing voices crying out in agony,

30
00:06:11,097 --> 00:06:15,097
I feel simply, overwhelmingly sad.

31
00:06:19,097 --> 00:06:22,097
Sir, here's the Transwanderous Nail.

32
00:06:22,097 --> 00:06:24,097
Good, put him through.

33
00:06:24,097 --> 00:06:28,097
Am I speaking with the Captain of the Amigo Pirates, Captain Largo?

34
00:06:28,097 --> 00:06:33,097
No, this is Vice Captain Colt, but I'm speaking on behalf of Captain Largo.

35
00:06:33,097 --> 00:06:44,097
Very well. This call is to inform you that Captain Siki has decided to accept Mr. Largo into his assembly as our 51st Pirate Captain. Congratulations.

36
00:06:44,097 --> 00:06:47,097
Well, of course.

37
00:06:47,097 --> 00:06:50,097
However, there is one condition.

38
00:06:50,097 --> 00:06:54,097
A mere formality that must be completed before you join.

39
00:06:54,097 --> 00:06:55,097
Oh!

40
00:06:56,097 --> 00:06:57,097
Un condition?

41
00:06:57,097 --> 00:07:08,097
Still no bites.

42
00:07:08,097 --> 00:07:10,097
Where are you fish?

43
00:07:10,097 --> 00:07:15,097
Man, I'm hungry.

44
00:07:15,097 --> 00:07:20,097
You don't say, cause you look pretty full to me.

45
00:07:20,097 --> 00:07:29,097
Well, we have been eating giant banquets every night. Our stomach's expanded. And as a result, we need to eat more to fill them up.

46
00:07:29,097 --> 00:07:34,097
Oh, I know. It's ridiculous how heavy my bones have gotten these past few days.

47
00:07:34,097 --> 00:07:36,097
That is not how it works.

48
00:07:36,097 --> 00:07:38,097
How's it going? Catch anything yet?

49
00:07:38,097 --> 00:07:40,097
Not yet. Not even a nibble.

50
00:07:40,097 --> 00:07:45,097
We're completely out of food, you know. Either you catch something or we don't eat.

51
00:07:45,097 --> 00:07:46,097
What?

52
00:07:46,097 --> 00:07:54,097
Yeah, what? I kept telling you guys we didn't have enough food to do banquets every damn night. But you had to party.

53
00:07:54,097 --> 00:07:57,097
Is that what we did?

54
00:07:57,097 --> 00:07:58,097
Yeah.

55
00:07:58,097 --> 00:08:00,097
Bunch of gluttons.

56
00:08:00,097 --> 00:08:02,097
Huh?

57
00:08:02,097 --> 00:08:08,097
Oh, a bite! A bite! A bite! I caught a bite!

58
00:08:08,097 --> 00:08:11,097
Oh, reel it in! Nicely cut, bro!

59
00:08:11,097 --> 00:08:20,097
It's a big sucker!

60
00:08:20,097 --> 00:08:23,097
Awesome! We're having a banquet tonight!

61
