182
00:15:26,097 --> 00:15:27,097
Come on, I didn't know you were that Beetle's owner!

183
00:15:28,097 --> 00:15:29,097
What owner?

184
00:15:29,097 --> 00:15:30,097
He's my friend!

185
00:15:30,097 --> 00:15:31,097
Nobody owns Boss!

186
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:33,097
Your friend?

187
00:15:34,097 --> 00:15:36,097
Really? You're already on someone else's team then?

188
00:15:37,097 --> 00:15:39,097
Don't you think he'd be better off on a real crew?

189
00:15:39,097 --> 00:15:43,097
No, he wouldn't! Because Boss and I are inseparable!

190
00:15:50,097 --> 00:15:52,097
Okay, can't argue with that!

191
00:15:58,097 --> 00:16:00,097
Here we go!

192
00:16:01,097 --> 00:16:02,097
Hey! What are you doing to him?

193
00:16:10,097 --> 00:16:11,097
Whoa!

194
00:16:13,097 --> 00:16:14,097
He's free!

195
00:16:16,097 --> 00:16:18,097
Sorry if I hurt you, big guy!

196
00:16:19,097 --> 00:16:21,097
You don't think he could hurt Boss, do you?

197
00:16:22,097 --> 00:16:24,097
What? I didn't mean it like that!

198
00:16:26,097 --> 00:16:27,097
Hey, are you okay?

199
00:16:28,097 --> 00:16:29,097
Hey!

200
00:16:30,097 --> 00:16:32,097
These wounds are nothing more than a few scratches to Boss!

201
00:16:33,097 --> 00:16:35,097
They'll all heal up while he's sleeping underground tonight!

202
00:16:36,097 --> 00:16:37,097
Wow! That's pretty badass!

203
00:16:37,097 --> 00:16:39,097
Oh yeah, you think that's cool?

204
00:16:40,097 --> 00:16:41,097
Well, he's gonna molt tomorrow too!

205
00:16:42,097 --> 00:16:44,097
He'll get even bigger and stronger than he is now!

206
00:16:45,097 --> 00:16:48,097
Huh. I didn't think Beetles kept on molting after they were fully grown.

207
00:16:49,097 --> 00:16:50,097
Boss isn't an ordinary Beetle.

208
00:16:51,097 --> 00:16:53,097
He sheds his skin once a month no matter how large he gets.

209
00:16:54,097 --> 00:16:56,097
So as big as he is, he's only gonna get bigger.

210
00:16:57,097 --> 00:16:59,097
He's gonna be even stronger than he is now?

211
00:17:00,097 --> 00:17:02,097
Sure is! What, do you wanna fight about it?

212
00:17:03,097 --> 00:17:04,097
Yeah! That's cool!

213
00:17:04,097 --> 00:17:07,097
Listen! I'll come back tomorrow and we'll try again!

214
00:17:08,097 --> 00:17:09,097
Uh!

215
00:17:10,097 --> 00:17:12,097
Then we'll know for sure which one of us is the strongest!

216
00:17:13,097 --> 00:17:14,097
But that's just ridiculous!

217
00:17:14,097 --> 00:17:15,097
Uh!

218
00:17:15,097 --> 00:17:16,097
No!

219
00:17:16,097 --> 00:17:17,097
No!

220
00:17:17,097 --> 00:17:18,097
No!

221
00:17:18,097 --> 00:17:19,097
No!

222
00:17:20,097 --> 00:17:21,097
Huh?

223
00:17:22,097 --> 00:17:24,097
All right!

224
00:17:25,097 --> 00:17:26,097
You better not chicken out on me then!

225
00:17:27,097 --> 00:17:28,097
Ha ha ha ha ha!

226
00:17:28,097 --> 00:17:35,097
If nothing else, the boy sure is spirited, isn't he?

227
00:17:36,097 --> 00:17:37,097
Boss?

228
00:17:43,097 --> 00:17:44,097
Watch your step!

229
00:17:45,097 --> 00:17:48,097
Wow! This cave is so cavernous!

230
00:17:49,097 --> 00:17:50,097
What's it used for?

231
00:17:51,097 --> 00:17:52,097
Oh, this? It's an escape route.

232
00:17:53,097 --> 00:17:54,097
From what?

233
00:17:54,097 --> 00:17:59,097
Well, this cave is like a massive labyrinth if you don't know your way around, so it's the perfect strategy for outrunning marauding pirates.

234
00:18:00,097 --> 00:18:03,097
We'd be hard pressed to find anyone more adept at running away than we are.

235
00:18:04,097 --> 00:18:05,097
And that's something you're proud of?

236
00:18:05,097 --> 00:18:08,097
That's the only way we can survive on the Grand Line.

237
00:18:09,097 --> 00:18:10,097
We don't have a military.

238
00:18:10,097 --> 00:18:16,097
And the island is so remote that the Navy basically treats us like we don't even exist, so we're on our own.

239
00:18:17,097 --> 00:18:20,097
Hey, speaking of the Navy, I noticed that girl was dressed up like a Marine.

240
00:18:23,097 --> 00:18:24,097
What's that all about?

241
00:18:26,097 --> 00:18:27,097
She wears that hat and coat.

242
00:18:28,097 --> 00:18:29,097
In memory of her father.

243
00:18:31,097 --> 00:18:33,097
That man was as good as they come.

244
00:18:33,097 --> 00:18:41,097
He refused to look the other way while we kept getting attacked, so he left his battalion and stayed on our island in order to protect us.

245
00:18:42,097 --> 00:18:44,097
And when you said, in memory of?

246
00:18:45,097 --> 00:18:46,097
It happened five long years ago.

247
00:18:47,097 --> 00:18:53,097
The poor brave man took on a group of pirates all by himself, and he was killed.

248
00:18:54,097 --> 00:19:00,097
And then three years later, Boss appeared out of nowhere as if this was his home.

249
00:19:00,097 --> 00:19:02,097
Yoko was the first to find him.

250
00:19:03,097 --> 00:19:04,097
They bonded right away.

251
00:19:05,097 --> 00:19:08,097
And he quickly became the guardian angel of our island.

252
00:19:09,097 --> 00:19:14,097
Truth be told, I get the impression that Boss's strength and bravery remind poor little Yoko of her father.

253
00:19:14,097 --> 00:19:17,097
Are you sure it's all right for us to be here?

254
00:19:18,097 --> 00:19:19,097
We are pirates.

255
00:19:20,097 --> 00:19:21,097
A different class of pirate.

256
00:19:22,097 --> 00:19:23,097
Now, here we are.

257
00:19:23,097 --> 00:19:24,097
Whoa!

258
00:19:24,097 --> 00:19:25,097
A windmill!

259
00:19:25,097 --> 00:19:26,097
It's huge!

260
00:19:26,097 --> 00:19:27,097
We're so high up!

261
00:19:27,097 --> 00:19:28,097
Whoa!

262
00:19:28,097 --> 00:19:32,097
I thought we were just going to get more rocks, but it's actually beautiful back here.

263
00:19:32,097 --> 00:19:33,097
Well, then again, not to be rude, but there's not much of an architectural uniformity here.

264
00:19:33,097 --> 00:19:34,097
It's interesting though.

265
00:19:34,097 --> 00:19:35,097
You don't recognize the theme?

266
00:19:35,097 --> 00:19:36,097
What?

267
00:19:36,097 --> 00:19:37,097
I don't know.

268
00:19:37,097 --> 00:19:38,097
I don't know.

269
00:19:38,097 --> 00:19:39,097
We're so high up!

270
00:19:39,097 --> 00:19:40,097
Whoa!

271
00:19:40,097 --> 00:19:43,097
I thought we were just going to get more rocks, but it's actually beautiful back here.

272
00:19:43,097 --> 00:19:58,097
Well, then again, not to be rude, but there's not much of an architectural uniformity here.

273
00:19:59,097 --> 00:20:00,097
It's interesting though.

274
00:20:00,097 --> 00:20:03,097
You don't recognize the theme?

275
00:20:03,097 --> 00:20:09,097
It was a deserted island when we came here, so we worked hard to make all the buildings look just like they do.

276
00:20:09,097 --> 00:20:16,097
The strange thing is that everyone who's landed here since has come from the same ocean, so our town is like a microcosm in a way.

277
00:20:17,097 --> 00:20:24,097
So we'd like to welcome you, Straw Hats, to Consorn Island, home away from home for expatriates of the East Blue.

278
00:20:25,097 --> 00:20:28,097
We like to call it Little East Blue.

279
00:20:28,097 --> 00:20:30,097
Yay!

280
00:20:30,097 --> 00:20:31,097
Wow!

281
00:20:31,097 --> 00:20:35,097
I never dreamed we'd have the East Blue's most famous rookies show up on our shore.

282
00:20:35,097 --> 00:20:36,097
Hey, Zoro.

283
00:20:36,097 --> 00:20:37,097
You're from Frost Moon Village, right?

284
00:20:37,097 --> 00:20:39,097
We've got a dojo just like the one you trained in.

285
00:20:39,097 --> 00:20:41,097
You should come and check it out.

286
00:20:41,097 --> 00:20:42,097
Really?

287
00:20:42,097 --> 00:20:44,097
And you grew up on the Baratie, right Sanji?

288
00:20:44,097 --> 00:20:47,097
We'd love to hear what you think of the food in our Baratie.

289
00:20:47,097 --> 00:20:48,097
It's pretty good.

290
00:20:48,097 --> 00:20:50,097
There's a Baratie here?

291
00:20:50,097 --> 00:20:52,097
Anyone here from Syrup Village?

292
00:20:52,097 --> 00:20:53,097
Let's see.

293
00:20:53,097 --> 00:20:55,097
I think Luigia might be from there, actually.

294
00:20:55,097 --> 00:20:56,097
Luigia?

295
00:20:56,097 --> 00:20:57,097
Yeah, that's right.

296
00:20:57,097 --> 00:20:59,097
She lives in the biggest mansion in town.

297
00:20:59,097 --> 00:21:00,097
A mansion?

298
00:21:00,097 --> 00:21:04,097
But the only mansion in Syrup Village is the one Kaya lives in.

299
00:21:08,097 --> 00:21:13,097
Everybody thinks they're so great, but no shifty pirate's gonna trick me.

300
00:21:13,097 --> 00:21:14,097
I swear it.

301
00:21:14,097 --> 00:21:15,097
It's been a while.

302
00:21:15,097 --> 00:21:17,097
Do you think they're okay?

303
00:21:17,097 --> 00:21:20,097
Don't get so worked up, Chopper.

304
00:21:20,097 --> 00:21:22,097
I'm sure they'll call us soon.

305
00:21:22,097 --> 00:21:23,097
Yeah, I hope so.

306
00:21:23,097 --> 00:21:27,097
You might want to think about building an insect cage for when they return, Frankie.

307
00:21:27,097 --> 00:21:28,097
Hey, good idea.

308
00:21:28,097 --> 00:21:31,097
I guess we're gonna need one if that thing's our new shipmate.

309
00:21:31,097 --> 00:21:33,097
You see?

310
00:21:33,097 --> 00:21:34,097
Click.

311
00:21:34,097 --> 00:21:35,097
It's me, Usopp.

312
00:21:35,097 --> 00:21:36,097
I need to talk to Nami.

313
00:21:36,097 --> 00:21:37,097
Hey, Usopp.

314
00:21:37,097 --> 00:21:38,097
It's Nami.

315
00:21:38,097 --> 00:21:39,097
What's going on?

316
00:21:39,097 --> 00:21:40,097
Did you guys catch it okay?

317
00:21:40,097 --> 00:21:41,097
No, no, no.

318
00:21:41,097 --> 00:21:42,097
Forget about that.

319
00:21:42,097 --> 00:21:44,097
Will you shut up and calm down?

320
00:21:44,097 --> 00:21:46,097
I can't hear her.

321
00:21:46,097 --> 00:21:49,097
Look, how quickly do you think you could get over to where we are?

322
00:21:49,097 --> 00:21:50,097
Huh?

323
00:21:50,097 --> 00:21:53,097
There's a town right on the other side of the island.

324
00:21:53,097 --> 00:21:54,097
Wait, give me the boat.

325
00:21:54,097 --> 00:21:55,097
She's coming.

326
00:21:55,097 --> 00:21:56,097
Hey, get easy, guys.

327
00:21:56,097 --> 00:21:57,097
I said I'd ask her, didn't I?

328
00:21:57,097 --> 00:21:58,097
I'm so confused.

329
00:21:58,097 --> 00:21:59,097
Please, just get over here.

330
00:21:59,097 --> 00:22:00,097
I'm begging you.

331
00:22:00,097 --> 00:22:01,097
Wait, why, Usopp?

332
00:22:01,097 --> 00:22:02,097
He hung up on me.

333
00:22:02,097 --> 00:22:03,097
Why do they just want you to come?

334
00:22:03,097 --> 00:22:04,097
I don't know.

335
00:22:04,097 --> 00:22:07,097
Well, I guess I might as well see what they want.

336
00:22:20,097 --> 00:22:22,097
You guys take care of the ship?

337
00:22:22,097 --> 00:22:23,097
Yeah, you got it.

338
00:22:25,097 --> 00:22:27,097
And there she goes.

339
00:22:31,097 --> 00:22:32,097
Is this it?

340
00:22:32,097 --> 00:22:34,097
It matches the description they gave.

341
00:22:34,097 --> 00:22:36,097
Rock-bound and surrounded by reefs.

342
00:22:36,097 --> 00:22:39,097
A natural barricade that can support your ships.

343
00:22:39,097 --> 00:22:41,097
Well, that's easy.

344
00:22:41,097 --> 00:22:44,097
No reefs are going to slow down this ship.

345
00:22:44,097 --> 00:22:50,097
All right, it's time to go hunting, boys.

346
00:22:50,097 --> 00:22:54,097
Let's grab the giant beetle that escaped from Shiki's hideout.

347
00:22:54,097 --> 00:22:57,097
Now, are you ready to catch a bug?

348
00:22:57,097 --> 00:22:59,097
See you!

349
00:23:06,097 --> 00:23:10,097
The Straw Hats have landed on an island where settlers from the East Blue live.

350
00:23:10,097 --> 00:23:14,097
Surrounded by familiar sights, they're suddenly reminded of home,

351
00:23:14,097 --> 00:23:16,097
even in faraway waters.

352
00:23:16,097 --> 00:23:19,097
However, the peaceful settlement is soon disrupted from an attack

353
00:23:19,097 --> 00:23:21,097
by the Amigo Pirates.

354
00:23:21,097 --> 00:23:23,097
On the next, One Piece,

355
00:23:23,097 --> 00:23:25,097
with a special presentation related to the movie,

356
00:23:25,097 --> 00:23:27,097
Little East Blue in Danger.

357
00:23:27,097 --> 00:23:30,097
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

